9. FINANCIAL DRAFT → REVIEW → PUBLISH SYSTEM

This workflow is mandatory.

Never automatically publish newly created financial records.

Follow this exact process:

Step 1 — Create Draft

When an Admin enters a new deposit or expense, save it as a private draft.

Step 2 — Review

Admin checks and validates the transaction.

Step 3 — Edit

Admin may correct the information before publishing.

Step 4 — Publish

An authorized Admin explicitly clicks the Publish button.

Step 5 — Public Display

Only published transactions are included in public financial totals and public transaction history.

Step 6 — Unpublish

An authorized Admin may unpublish a previously published transaction.

The public totals must recalculate accordingly.

Important rules

- New entries must not change public financial totals before publication.
- Draft records must remain private.
- Rejected records must remain private.
- Unpublished records must remain private.
- Editing or deleting records must preserve audit history.
- Never silently erase financial history.
- Require confirmation before important financial actions.
- Record which Admin performed each action.

